SUDO
====

Run command with admin rights.


BASIC
-----
sudo command

Asks for password first.
Then runs command as admin.


EXAMPLE
-------
sudo apt-get update

Installs system updates.


WHEN TO USE
-----------
• Install software
• Edit system files
• Change permissions
• System administration


WARNING
-------
Be careful with sudo!
Wrong commands can break system.
Only use when necessary.


COMMON
------
sudo apt-get install    Install package (Linux)
sudo systemctl restart  Restart service
sudo cat /var/log/file  Read system logs
sudo rm -r folder       Delete as admin


PASSWORD
--------
Prompts for your password.
Nothing shows while typing.
Press Enter when done.


TIPS
----
Don't use sudo casually.
Understand what command does first.
Ask before using sudo if unsure.
